Refactor WTrader GUI handling to remove redundant automatic button/control discovery.

Context:
I already have another mod/project that contains the correct DonutSMP GUI/button detection mechanics, /home/the_cet/IT/WProject/WProtect-standalone/ find all related stuff for buttons ah etc


Goal:
Remove unnecessary WTrader code that tries to automatically infer, learn, discover, classify, or guess GUI buttons/actions.

Delete or simplify code related to:
- semantic button auto-detection
- GUI control inference
- automatic action classification from item type/name/lore
- learned button semantics
- heuristic detection of REFRESH / FILTER / BUY / CONFIRM / CANCEL
- GUI button discovery persistence
- confidence scoring for discovered controls
- auto-learning of button positions
- duplicate abstractions that only exist for automatic button discovery
- tests/fixtures that only test heuristic button detection

Do NOT remove:
- Mineflayer connection/runtime
- raw window/screen observation
- window open/close/update events
- slot snapshots
- changed-slot detection
- safe item/component parsing
- normalized readable window title parsing
- raw GUI/window IDs and types
- manual /gui, /slot, /click debug tooling
- guarded click execution
- inventory tracking
- purchase verification/reconciliation infrastructure
- market/pricing/risk/database/Redis code
- generic GameClientAdapter interfaces needed for execution

Keep GUI handling minimal and deterministic.

Desired architecture:

1. Game client layer only exposes raw/normalized facts:
   - window id
   - window type
   - normalized title
   - raw title
   - slot id
   - item fingerprint/data
   - slot updates
   - inventory updates

2. No guessing of what a button means.

3. Action mapping must come from an explicit external/static Donut GUI profile that will be ported from the other mod later.

Example future interface:

interface GuiProfile {
  matchesWindow(window): boolean
  listingSlots(window): number[]
  getActionSlot(action, window): number | null
  validateActionSlot(action, slot, window): boolean
}

Actions may include:
- REFRESH
- NEXT_PAGE
- PREVIOUS_PAGE
- FILTER
- CONFIRM_BUY
- CANCEL_BUY

But DO NOT implement heuristic detection for them now.

4. Remove code paths that persist or learn GUI semantics automatically.
If database tables/types exist only for auto-discovery, remove them only if clearly unused elsewhere.
If removing a DB migration would be unsafe, leave the schema but stop using it and mark it deprecated.

5. Keep safety validation:
Even when an explicit profile provides a slot, WTrader must still validate:
- expected window/title/type
- expected item/control fingerprint where configured
- expected slot exists
before clicking.

6. Do not touch trading strategy or protocol/network diagnostics.

7. After cleanup:
- remove dead imports/types/files
- remove obsolete tests
- add tests proving there is NO heuristic GUI action inference
- add tests for explicit profile-driven action lookup
- run lint
- run typecheck
- run tests
- run build

At the end, provide:
- deleted files/modules
- simplified modules
- deprecated DB/schema pieces
- remaining GUI execution flow
- anything that still looks like redundant auto-discovery code